Add `ReprAttr::ReprCpp` variant so the attribute survives from the
parser all the way to layout / codegen.

`ReprCpp` semantically implies the C layout constraints (field
order preserved, no Rust-reordering) plus the extended Itanium C++
ABI rules (sret for non-trivial-for-calls classes, this-pointer
prepending). The actual behavior lives in P05 (ReprOptions flag
threading) and P06 (layout delegation); this patch just lets the
variant exist.

diff --git a/compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs b/compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs
--- a/compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs
@@ -169,6 +169,12 @@ pub enum ReprAttr {
     ReprInt(IntType),
     ReprRust,
     ReprC,
+    /// `#[repr(cpp)]`. Implies C-compatible layout plus the
+    /// extended Itanium C++ ABI rules: sret for non-trivial-for-
+    /// calls classes, explicit `this`-pointer on methods, and
+    /// Itanium-style name mangling for items whose `extern` is
+    /// `"C++"`. See `rustcc`'s `fork/PATCHES.md`.
+    ReprCpp,
     ReprPacked(Align),
     ReprSimd,
     ReprTransparent,
